course: dictionary
lesson: 7675
title: Who owns it? The proprietor
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A proprietor is the owner of something, often a business. You might see the word on a shop sign: «J. Smith, Proprietor». The sign tells you that J. Smith owns the shop.
explain: Proprietor is a formal word. In everyday talk, people say owner instead. If you are not sure, swap in owner and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: The word can also mean an owner of land or property. In a famous story, «Toad, a landed proprietor» means Toad owns land, so landed here means he owns a lot of land. Context clues like this help you work out a new word.
fact: A proprietor is the owner of a business, such as a shop, hotel, restaurant or newspaper.
fact: A proprietor can also be the owner of property, such as land.
fact: «Sole proprietor» means one person who owns the business alone. Sole means only one.
fact: «Proprietor» is a formal word, and everyday speech usually says «owner».
fact: Look for clues like a shop sign or the word «of» to find out what someone owns: «the proprietor of the hotel» means the owner of the hotel.
exercise: «J. Smith, Proprietor» is written on the shop door. What is a proprietor? | A worker who sweeps the floor | A sign painter | *The owner of the shop | A customer who buys things
exercise: «The sole proprietor of the bakery baked bread at dawn.» Which word means only one? | baked | *sole | dawn | bakery
exercise: «Toad, a landed proprietor» owns land. What does landed proprietor mean? | A lazy visitor | A person who sells newspapers | *A landowner | A sailor on a boat
test: «The proprietor of the café wiped the tables before opening.» Who is the proprietor? | A customer waiting for a table | *The owner of the café | A street sweeper | The cook who makes the cakes
test: In everyday speech, which word would most people use instead of proprietor? | *Owner | Guest | Customer | Boss of the bus
exam: A shop proprietor buys 5 bags of rice and sells them for a profit. In this maths problem, who is the proprietor? | A delivery driver | A maths teacher | *The owner of the business | A bag of rice
